# AgentMux is developed on Windows and built and run inside WSL. Without a
# declared normalisation the same file can land in the repository with CRLF on
# one machine and LF on the other, which breaks shell scripts and produces
# noisy diffs.
#
# Everything textual is stored with LF and checked out with LF, on every
# platform. Go, TypeScript, SQL, and Markdown do not care; shell scripts and
# tmux-adjacent files very much do.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary assets must never be line-ending converted.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.ico binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary

# Lockfiles are generated; keep them out of diff review noise.
web/package-lock.json -diff linguist-generated
